Average total article quality scores based on the QUADS rating scale were 32.3 ± 0.2 (range 22–38). Individual item scores were high for most aspects under consideration, with average scores for 11 of the 13 items being appraised as 2.5 or greater. Individual items scores were poor for two aspects: (i) consideration of stakeholders in the research design or conduct (0.7 ± 0.1) and (ii) critical discussion of strengths and limitations (2.0 ± 0.2).

